{
  "id": "task_003",
  "title": "LFU Cache",
  "language": "javascript",
  "difficulty": "hard",
  "source": "LeetCode #460",
  "description": "Implement an LFU (Least Frequently Used) cache in JavaScript named `LFUCache`.\n\n`constructor(capacity)` sets the capacity. `get(key)` returns the value or -1. `put(key, value)` inserts/updates. When the cache is full, evict the LEAST FREQUENTLY USED key; if several keys tie on use-count, evict the LEAST RECENTLY USED among them. Both `get` and `put` count as a use of the key. If `capacity` is 0 the cache stores nothing. Both operations must run in O(1) average time.\n\nclass LFUCache {\n  constructor(capacity) {}\n  get(key) {}\n  put(key, value) {}\n}",
  "function_signature": "class LFUCache { constructor(capacity) {} get(key) {} put(key, value) {} }",
  "constraints": [
    "0 <= capacity <= 10^4",
    "0 <= key, value <= 10^5",
    "get and put run in O(1) average time"
  ],
